course: dictionary
lesson: 9830
title: Swelling: bigger, puffier, louder
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Swelling is a word with more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one you need. «A sling holds the arm up against the body so it can rest and the swelling goes down.» Here swelling is a part of the body that has become puffy and bigger. When the swelling goes down, the puffiness gets smaller.
explain: «The river is swelling after the rain» uses swelling as a doing word: the river is getting bigger. «Music swelling» means the music is getting louder and stronger. Ask yourself: what is getting bigger, a body part or a thing growing?
explain: Read the words around it. «A sting inside the mouth or throat is dangerous because the swelling can block breathing.» The clue is block breathing, so this swelling is serious. Swap in a meaning to check it: a puffy lump can block breathing, so the meaning fits.
fact: Swelling can be a noun, as in «a swelling on the ankle», or the -ing form of the verb swell.
fact: «Swelling» can mean a part of the body that has become bigger and puffy, often after a bump, a sprain, a sting or an infection.
fact: «Swelling» can also mean getting bigger or louder, as in «the river is swelling» or «music swelling».
fact: For a bump or sprain, rest, a cold pack wrapped in a cloth, and raising the hurt part can help the swelling go down.
fact: Swelling of the face, lips or tongue after a sting or food can be a serious allergic reaction, so get help immediately.
exercise: «A sling holds the arm up so the swelling goes down.» What does swelling mean here? | *A part of the body that has become puffy and bigger | Getting louder and stronger | A ringing sound in the ears | A big meal at a party
exercise: «The river is swelling after the heavy rain.» What does swelling mean here? | Getting louder | *Getting bigger | Going to sleep | A part of the body that hurts
exercise: «A sting inside the mouth or throat is dangerous because the swelling can block breathing.» Why is this swelling serious? | It makes the lips look pink | It only lasts a minute | It is only a little itchy | *It can block breathing
test: «Doctors treated the swelling after the rattlesnake bite.» In this sentence, swelling is a: | verb | pronoun | adverb | *noun
test: Which phrase means the puffiness is getting smaller? | *The swelling goes down | The swelling goes sideways | Swelling up
exam: Ben says, «The swelling goes down with rest and a cold pack wrapped in a cloth.» What should Ben do to help a swollen ankle? | Shake the ankle hard | *Rest it and use a cold pack wrapped in a cloth | Run a race to get the blood moving | Eat a large meal and wait
